BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    led as it flowed across, becoming three jars for the second village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (  The second village, seeing this gift, faced a choice. They could keep all three jars, or honor) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (     the trust shown to them. Remembering that fortune turns like seasons, they poured back two ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (    jars into the fountain-one for the gift received, one for the trust given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
