BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  In the beginning, two spirits dwelled in the mountains: Sendara of the Highland Spring and Rec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    ivos of the Valley Pool. Each possessed life-giving water, but only Sendara's spring flowed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    freely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  The Goddess of Abundance appeared to Sendara, saying: "Whatever water you send downstream, I s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    hall triple it before it reaches Recivos.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  Sendara pondered deeply. Hoarding all the water would leave her neighbor dry and hostile. She ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    decided to send half her waters down the mountain. The Goddess blessed it, and three times t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    hat amount reached Recivos's valley.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  Recivos rejoiced at the abundance. He understood that Sendara had sacrificed her own reserves ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    from trust. In gratitude, he sent back half of what he received, ensuring Sendara gained mor) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    e than she had given, while he still prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  Season after season, this sacred exchange continued. Both spirits flourished beyond what eithe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    r could achieve alone.) Tj ET
