BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      In the beginning, two spirits dwelled in the mountains: Sendara of the Highland Spring and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (         Recivos of the Valley Pool. Each possessed life-giving water, but only Sendara's spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (         flowed freely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      The Goddess of Abundance appeared to Sendara, saying: "Whatever water you send downstream,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (         I shall triple it before it reaches Recivos.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      Sendara pondered deeply. Hoarding all the water would leave her neighbor dry and hostile. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        She decided to send half her waters down the mountain. The Goddess blessed it, and three) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (         times that amount reached Recivos's valley.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      Recivos rejoiced at the abundance. He understood that Sendara had sacrificed her own reser) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        ves from trust. In gratitude, he sent back half of what he received, ensuring Sendara ga) Tj ET
