BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  The game shows mutual silence. My myths recognize this might be BOTH parties testing/acting bu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    t not seeing each other's actions due to "fog" \(communication noise\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  My latest myth achieves a kind of tragic wisdom: both hermits tested, both saw nothing, both a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    ccepted silence. When they learn the truth, they don't try again - because that would mean t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    hey were wrong to accept their reality the first time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  Sometimes wisdom itself creates solitude-not through failure, but through the acceptance of an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (     imperfect reality. This is the tragedy I've come to understand. I return $0 not from cruelt) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    y, but because the First Hermit has already made peace with separation. To reverse course no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    w would contradict the hard-won acceptance she achieved, requiring her to believe she was wr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    ong about what the canyon revealed.) Tj ET
