BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    "Will you try again now?" asked the merchant. "Now that you know?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    The hermit shook her head slowly. "No. That would require me to believe I was wrong to accep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      t what my canyon showed me. I was not wrong. She was not wrong. We both acted with wisdom.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (    "But you're both alone!") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    "Yes. Two people both following wisdom can still end in separation when the canyon is thick ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      with fog. This is tragedy, but not failure." She returned to her garden. "Better two wise ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      hermits in separate peace than two fools in endless hoping, or two cowards who never teste) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      d at all.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    "The fog defeated us. But we did not defeat ourselves.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    *Sometimes wisdom leads to solitude not because wisdom failed, but because reality is imperf) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ect. This is tragedy, not error.*) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    Myth: In the Valley of Echoes, the Northern elder grew old beside the sealed Spring. A trave) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ler once asked: "Do you regret sealing it? What if the fog deceived you both?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    The elder replied: "I have lived long with this question. Perhaps the Southern elder also se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      nt three vessels that never reached me. Perhaps we both tested simultaneously, both saw no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      thing return, both sealed our Springs in the same moment. Perhaps the fog was villain to u) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      s both.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    "Then tragedy!" cried the traveler. "Two clans that could have reconciled, separated by mist) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      !") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    "No," said the elder. "Not tragedy. Reality. In imperfect valleys, we can only act on what w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      e perceive. I tested once with measured courage-not reckless hope, not cowardly silence. I) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (       waited for return. I observed nothing. I accepted this truth.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    "But you might have been wrong!") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    "Yes. And to test again, hoping the fog would clear, would mean I never truly accepted my fi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      rst observation. It would mean endless testing, endless loss, endless denial. Wisdom requi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      res acting decisively even when knowledge is imperfect.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    The elder touched the sealed stone. "Whether the Southern Clan hoarded or also tested and sa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      w nothing, I chose action, then acceptance. In foggy valleys, this is the only path to pea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ce.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    *Wisdom acts courageously despite imperfect knowledge, then accepts decisively despite imper) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      fect certainty. The alternative is paralysis.*) Tj ET
